{"id": "striviaqa0053", "pool": "striviaqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2712938540, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0a50579e3e6d4e8f80f3a27fbf2102252cfeb0b6531aaa3ed4093fb37d776cc0", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Which Kent brewer is believed to be the oldest continuous brewer in the country?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/striviaqa0053.wav", "input_sha256": "6fc2b919a86ee03aa47b09b744a1fbee538a7dec197fbea534b3f6dae6dc7556", "input_samples": 74766, "input_s": 4.673, "n_real_chunks": 5, "score": 0.8934, "act": 0.9999, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "False. Shepherd Neame is generally identified as Britain’s oldest brewer, tracing its history to 1698. Wychwood Brewery was much newer and, in fact, its Witney brewery closed in 2023, with beer production transferred elsewhere. (shepherdneame.co.uk)", "expert_answer": "False.\n\n**Shepherd Neame** is generally identified as **Britain’s oldest brewer**, tracing its history to **1698**. Wychwood Brewery was much newer and, in fact, its Witney brewery closed in **2023**, with beer production transferred elsewhere. ([shepherdneame.co.uk](https://www.shepherdneame.co.uk/about-us?utm_source=openai))", "transcript": "Wychwood Brewery is believed to be the oldest continuous brewer in the country.\n", "asr_s": 1.36, "expert_s": 6.53, "expert_input_samples": 74766, "expert_input_s": 4.673, "expert_input_sha256": "6fc2b919a86ee03aa47b09b744a1fbee538a7dec197fbea534b3f6dae6dc7556", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 6.646, "relay_synth_ms": 17836, "onset_chunk": 5, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/striviaqa/audio/striviaqa0053_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "50